# Confirm Dialog (Delete / Confirmation) – Visual Reference

Reference: `src/components/ui/ConfirmDialog.jsx` and `src/components/ui/Modal.jsx`. Use when building or changing confirmation/delete dialogs so they stay consistent.

---

## 1. Modal wrapper (Modal.jsx)

| Property | Value |
|----------|--------|
| Overlay | `fixed inset-0 z-50 flex items-center justify-center p-4` |
| Backdrop | `fixed inset-0 bg-black/70` (click closes) |
| Content box | `relative z-10 bg-white rounded-xl shadow-lg border border-gray-200 p-5 max-w-lg w-full overflow-hidden` |

---

## 2. ConfirmDialog content

| Property | Value |
|----------|--------|
| Container | `text-center sm:text-left` |
| Title | `text-xl font-semibold mb-2 text-charcoal` |
| Message | `text-gray-600 mb-6` |
| Buttons row | `flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 sm:justify-end` |

---

## 3. Buttons (outline only – no fill)

All buttons use **outline only** (rounded border, no background fill). Do not use filled/colored backgrounds.

**Cancel:**

- `px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border-2 border-gray-300 bg-white text-charcoal hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors order-2 sm:order-1`

**Confirm – non-destructive (e.g. "Activate", "Deactivate"):**

- `px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border-2 border-charcoal bg-white text-charcoal hover:bg-gray-50 transition-colors order-1 sm:order-2`

**Confirm – destructive (e.g. "Delete"):**

- `px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border-2 border-red-500 bg-white text-red-600 hover:bg-red-50 transition-colors order-1 sm:order-2`

---

## 4. Props

- `isOpen`, `onClose`, `onConfirm`, `title`, `message` – required
- `confirmText` – default `"OK"`; use action-specific label for clarity (e.g. `"Deactivate"`, `"Activate"`, `"Delete"`)
- `cancelText` – default `"Cancel"`
- `isDestructive` – default `false`; when `true`, confirm button uses red **outline** (border + text), not filled.

**Copy (title / message):**

- Title: sentence style, lowercase after the first word (e.g. "Deactivate location", "Delete agency").
- Message: clear question, e.g. `Are you sure you want to ${action} "${name}"?` for toggle; for delete add "This action cannot be undone."
- Confirm button label: match the action – "Deactivate", "Activate", or "Delete" – so the user sees exactly what they are confirming.

---

## 5. Summary

- Modal: white box, `rounded-xl`, `shadow-lg`, `border border-gray-200`, `max-w-lg`, `p-5`; backdrop `bg-black/70`.
- Title: `text-xl font-semibold text-charcoal`, `mb-2`.
- Message: `text-gray-600`, `mb-6`.
- **All buttons outline only** (no filled background): `rounded-lg`, `border-2`, `bg-white`, hover light tint.
- Cancel: `border-gray-300 text-charcoal hover:bg-gray-50`.
- Confirm (normal): `border-charcoal text-charcoal hover:bg-gray-50`.
- Confirm (destructive): `border-red-500 text-red-600 hover:bg-red-50`.
- Order: on mobile confirm first, on desktop cancel left / confirm right.
